            "## Find out what the wall is made of\n"
            "Concrete, brick, plasterboard and wood need different fixings. There are special anchors for plasterboard; for a heavy painting on concrete, a wall plug and screw. If in doubt, ask at a hardware shop or a handyman, giving the painting’s weight and size.\n\n"
            "## Two fixings are safer than one\n"
            "A wide painting is easier to hang on two hooks — it won’t tilt. For small, light works one is enough.\n\n"
            "## Template and level\n"
            "Cut a paper template to the size of the painting, mark the hanging points and fix it to the wall. Level it (a phone app will do). Drill right through the marks. That way you make exactly as many holes as you need.\n\n"
